subproblems.statement:
Let μ be a measure on ℝ^N, n ∈ ℕ and a ∈ [0,∞]. With R(y,ρ) := densityRatio n μ y ρ = μ(B_ρ(y))/(ω·ofReal(ρ)^n) (closed balls, ω = unitBallVolume n), suppose:
(i) μ(B_ρ(y)) < ∞ for all y ∈ ℝ^N and ρ ∈ ℝ;
(ii) for every y, ρ ↦ R(y,ρ) is non-decreasing on (0,∞);
(iii) for μ-a.e. y there is θ ∈ [0,∞] with HasDensity n μ y θ (Θ^n(μ,y) exists and equals θ) and a ≤ θ.
Then a ≤ R(y,ρ) for every y in the support spt μ and every ρ > 0.
